      "cr": 0,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Iochi Mari.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 0 as a student. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>Sisterhood Club / The One Who Actually Quiets The Room</strong> — Trinity General School, Classroom 2-B; the Sisterhood Club</p><p>Status: Active — student, Classroom 2-B; Sisterhood Club representative</p><p>Mari is the student who welcomed the advisor formally, offered the Sisterhood Club's help before being asked, and then quietly got the classroom under control when shouting had failed. She sits with good posture, laces her fingers on the desk, and tucks a strand of hair behind her ear before she says anything that matters. She is also the person who translated SCHALE into plain language for the students who were too embarrassed to admit they did not understand it.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Club</strong> — “Sisterhood Club / The One Who Actually Quiets The Room”</li><li><strong>Silver Tongue</strong> — “When the room had descended into outfit requests and snack negotiations, Mari raised her hand — though she had already been looking at him — and asked the only question in the session that went to the point: &quot;I think”</li><li><strong>Mechanical Aptitude</strong> — “People don't care about gadgets or uniforms.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/iochi_mari</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/iochi_mari</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
